  "text-ergebnisse.tex": {
   "lines": [
    "The specimen reached a tensile strength of \\labval{tensile-test-synthetische-kurve}{Rm} (maximum force \\labval{tensile-test-synthetische-kurve}{Fmax} after \\labval{tensile-test-synthetische-kurve}{tmax}). Yield onset was at \\labval{tensile-test-synthetische-kurve}{yield}; the ratio of maximum to yield onset was \\labval{tensile-test-synthetische-kurve}{ratio}. From the maximum to the break the load dropped by \\labval{tensile-test-synthetische-kurve}{drop}; it stayed above 90\\,\\% of the maximum for \\labval{tensile-test-synthetische-kurve}{hold}. Compared with the reference material EN AW-5052-H38 ($R_m = $ \\labval{tensile-test-synthetische-kurve}{refRm} \\cite{mat-en-aw-5052-h38}), the tensile strength deviates by \\labval{tensile-test-synthetische-kurve}{refdRm}. Agreement in $R_m$ alone does not identify the material. The apparent modulus of \\labval{tensile-test-synthetische-kurve}{E} is not a material property."
   ],
   "type": "tex"
  },
  "text-methodik.tex": {
   "lines": [
    "The dataset ``Synthetische Kurve'' (version 1) \\cite{data-tensile-test-synthetische-kurve} of a specimen Manuell, b = --, Dicke -- was evaluated, with the columns Spannung [MPa] and Dehnung [\\%]. The time axis of the evaluation was calculated from the travelled displacement and the test speed \\labval{tensile-test-synthetische-kurve}{v}, so strain and modulus follow the measured displacement. Stress refers to the initial cross-section $A_0 = $\\labval{tensile-test-synthetische-kurve}{A0}. The linear section was determined as the longest time window in which the data points lie on a straight line within a fixed tolerance. Yield onset is the first point after this window that deviates from the extended line by more than \\labval{tensile-test-synthetische-kurve}{thr} of the maximum. This threshold is a convention, not a proof stress $R_{p0.2}$. The measurement was compared with the 17 materials of the group Aluminium; their stress--strain curves are idealised from $R_{p0.2}$, $R_m$, $A$ and $E$ and are not measured curves (property values from~\\cite{mat-en-aw-1050a-weich,mat-en-aw-8011a-o-folie,mat-en-aw-1050a-h14,mat-en-aw-3003-h14,mat-en-aw-6060-t6,mat-en-aw-5754-o-h111,mat-en-aw-5052-h32,mat-en-aw-5754-h22,mat-en-aw-5052-h38,mat-en-aw-5086-h116-h32,mat-en-aw-5083-o-h111,mat-en-aw-6061-t6,mat-en-aw-6082-t6,mat-en-aw-7020-t6,mat-en-aw-2017a-t4,mat-en-aw-2024-t3,mat-en-aw-7075-t6})."
   ],
   "type": "tex"
  },
